{"tool_name":"modsara-variant","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"modsara-variant","home":"https://publichealth.yale.edu/c2s2/software/modSaRa/","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"modSaRa is an R package designed to perform copy number variants identification.","addition_date":"2018-09-03T17:17:43Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:59:01Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:modsara-variant","credit":[{"email":"heping.zhang@yale.edu","name":"Heping Zhang","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://publichealth.yale.edu/c2s2/software/modsara/Reference%20manual_291037_284_28429_v1.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genetic mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0282"}]}],"name":"modSaRa","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx212","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2017. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.Summary: Chromosomal copy number variation (CNV) refers to a polymorphism that a DNA segment presents deletion or duplication in the population. The computational algorithms developed to identify this type of variation are usually of high computational complexity. Here we present a user-friendly R package, modSaRa, designed to perform copy number variants identification. The package is developed based on a change-point based method with optimal computational complexity and desirable accuracy. The current version of modSaRa package is a comprehensive tool with integration of preprocessing steps and main CNV calling steps.","authors":[{"name":"Hao N."},{"name":"Jin Z."},{"name":"Niu Y."},{"name":"Xiao F."},{"name":"Xu Y."},{"name":"Zhang H."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2017-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"ModSaRa: A computationally effi